### Project ignores
tmp/

# Worktree-discipline pack — installed from the livespec-dev-tooling package
# (the single canonical source) into dev-tooling/ at bootstrap, NEVER tracked
# here, mirroring how the commit-refuse hooks are installed into the untracked
# shared .git/hooks/ dir. The pack is four files: the two executable shell
# scripts plus the `worktree.just` and `branch-protection.just` recipe
# fragments the root justfile `import?`s. `just bootstrap` materializes them
# via the `worktree-pack` LOCAL obligation row.
/dev-tooling/worktree-lib.sh
/dev-tooling/branch-protection.sh
/dev-tooling/worktree.just
/dev-tooling/branch-protection.just
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.idea/

### Python toolchain artifacts
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*

### UV local state
.venv/

### Beads / Dolt
# Per-clone bd state (Dolt working copy, lockfiles, runtime artifacts,
# per-machine metadata.json) is excluded by .beads/.gitignore (tracked
# itself, once the tenant is provisioned). `.beads/config.yaml` IS tracked:
# it carries the server-mode connection block for the livespec-driver-codex
# Dolt tenant with NO per-machine project_id and NO password (the tenant
# password is supplied via the BEADS_DOLT_PASSWORD env var at bd-call time).
# The beads tenant is DEFERRED to a later family-infra phase (see
# .livespec.jsonc), so no `.beads/` tree exists yet.
.beads-credential-key
*.env.local
